<title>UK: EBRD lends $90 million to Uzbek oil/gas firm.</title>
<headline>EBRD lends $90 million to Uzbek oil/gas firm.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Bank for Reconstruction and Development (EBRD) said on Monday it would lend $90 million to the National Corporation for Oil and Gas Industry of Uzbekistan (Uzbekneftegas).</p>
<p>The money will be used to upgrade the Fergana refinery to process domestic crude oil with a high sulphur content as well as improve safety and reduce pollution.</p>
<p>The EBRD is co-financing the $195.5 million project with the Export-Import Bank of Japan.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7770 (fax +44 171 583 7239)</p>
